Hi Peter,

The RefSeq annotation is very different from Gencode annotation. RefSeq annotation usually includes less exons and smaller total exon length for genes. So it is not surprising to see that gene has a smaller total exon length in RefSeq than in Encode.

Hopefully this answers your question. But let me know if doesnt.

Cheers,
Wei

